course: dictionary
lesson: 11307
title: Yearly: once every year
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Yearly means happening once every year. «At the yearly check-up a dog gets an injection» means the dog goes to the vet once each year for its check-up.
explain: Yearly can also mean for one whole year. In «a yearly cost», the cost is the total for a whole year. Read the words around it to see which meaning fits. Ask yourself: how often does this happen, or how long does it last?
explain: Yearly can describe a thing, as in «a yearly visit», or tell you how often something happens, as in «The school trip is held yearly». Annual means the same thing and is a more formal word.
fact: Yearly means happening once every year.
fact: «A salary is yearly pay», which means the money someone earns in one whole year.
fact: Yearly can be an adjective, as in «a yearly visit», or an adverb, as in «held yearly».
fact: Annual is a more formal word with the same meaning as yearly.
fact: In maths, a yearly amount can be turned into a monthly or weekly amount, or the other way round.
exercise: «At the yearly check-up a dog gets an injection.» What does yearly mean here? | Only once in a lifetime | Every hour | Only on a rainy day | *Once every year
exercise: A car needs a yearly safety test. What does yearly tell you about the test? | It costs nothing | *It is done once a year | Every week | It is done only in the morning
exercise: If someone's yearly pay is 12000 pounds, about how much is that each month? | 144000 pounds | 12000 pounds | 500 pounds | *1000 pounds
test: Which word means nearly the same as yearly, but is more formal? | Hourly | *Annual | Weekly | Daily
test: Aaliyah says, «The river flooded yearly.» What does yearly mean in her sentence? | *Once every year | Only once, and never again | Every minute | Very loudly
exam: Which sentence uses yearly as an adverb? | *The school trip is held yearly | We had a yearly visit to the zoo | A yearly subscription costs money | She reads a yearly magazine
